  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Given a permutation PPP of size NNN, an array AAA of size NNN can be generated using the following method:\n\n\nIf Pi&gt;PjP_i\\gt P_jPi​&gt;Pj​ for all (1≤j&lt;i)(1 \\leq j \\lt i)(1≤j&lt;i), set Ai=0A_i=0Ai​=0;\nOtherwise, set Ai=max(j)A_i = max(j)Ai​=max(j) where (1≤j&lt;i)(1 \\leq j \\lt i)(1≤j&lt;i) and (Pj&gt;Pi)(P_j \\gt P_i)(Pj​&gt;Pi​).\nUnfortunately, we lost the permutation PPP and some elements of the array AAA.\n\nThe lost elements of the array AAA are denoted as Ai=−1A_i = -1Ai​=−1. These elements can be replaced with any non-negative integer.\n\nGiven an array AAA with some lost elements, check whether there exists a permutation PPP, such that, we can obtain the array AAA from PPP using the above method.\n\nIf at least one such permutations exist, print the **lexicographically smallest** permutation.\n\nIf no such permutation exists, print −1-1−1 instead.\n\nNote:\n\n\nA permutation of size NNN contains each element from 111 to NNN exactly once.\nPermutation XXX is said to be lexicographically smaller than permutation YYY if:\n\nXi&lt;YiX_i \\lt Y_iXi​&lt;Yi​;\nXj=YjX_j = Y_jXj​=Yj​ for all (1≤j&lt;i)(1\\le j \\lt i)(1≤j&lt;i).\n\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains an integer NNN — the size of AAA.\nThe next line contains NNN space-separated integers: A1,A2,…,ANA_1,A_2,\\ldots ,A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line:\n\n\n\nIf at least one such permutations exist, print the **lexicographically smallest** permutation.\nIf no such permutation exists, print −1-1−1 instead.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤101 \\leq T \\leq 101≤T≤10",
      "1≤N≤2⋅1051 \\leq N \\leq 2\\cdot 10^51≤N≤2⋅105",
      "−1≤Ai&lt;N-1 \\leq A_i \\lt N−1≤Ai​&lt;N",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 2⋅1052\\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
